{% doc %}
  Moves a ticket to another status (05 §1). Refuses an unknown status.
  Copies the category, stamps solved_at/closed_at, clears needs_reply when
  solved. Any member who can reach the ticket may close it: the close is
  reversible and the activity log records who did it.

  New is a target like any other. new and open behave identically in
  helpers/categories, and the first-reply deadline gates on
  first_replied_at rather than the category, so returning a ticket to New
  cannot restart the SLA clock; support_ticket_created hangs off creation,
  so no new-ticket alert re-fires either.
  Build/Check/Execute: change_status/build, check, execute. Moving to the
  status the ticket already has changes nothing. Returns { valid, errors, ticket }.
  @param {object} ticket - Ticket loaded through queries/tickets/find
  @param {string} status_key - Target status key
  @param {object} actor - { type, id, member }
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign result = { "valid": false, "errors": {}, "ticket": null }
  function object = 'modules/support/commands/tickets/change_status/build', ticket: ticket, status_key: status_key, actor: actor
  function object = 'modules/support/commands/tickets/change_status/check', object: object
  unless object.valid
    assign result.errors = object.errors
    return result
  endunless
  if object.status.id == ticket.status_id
    assign result.valid = true
    assign result.ticket = ticket
    return result
  endif
  function saved = 'modules/support/commands/tickets/change_status/execute', object: object
  assign result.valid = true
  assign result.ticket = saved
  return result
%}
